  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LuciferGuard & Identity Security:\n      - Deprecated the legacy \"SessionManager\" (lifecycle-based) in favor of the new \"LuciferGuard\" (event-driven), achieving 0% idle CPU overhead.\n      - Standardized the Identity API: introduced \"CreateIdentity\", \"AuthenticateSession\", \"AuthorizeSession\", and \"ElevateRole\" for explicit identity lifecycle control.\n      - Optimized Lazy Identity Validation: security checks are now performed on-demand, improving cache locality and eliminating background scanning jitter.\n      - Implemented Single-Session Admin Enforcement: automatically disconnects stale physical sockets when an Admin authenticates from a new location.\n      - Enhanced Admin Protection: Admin identities now have a reduced TTL (2 hours) to enforce strict re-authentication and minimize compromise windows.\n\n      Infrastructure & Performance:\n      - Refactored the Authorization Pipeline: achieved near-zero allocation using Utf8Map and compiled expression trees for high-speed route execution.\n      - Improved Memory Efficiency: integrated \"IdentityRecord\" into LuciferPool to eliminate GC pressure during high authentication throughput.\n      - Naming Alignment: updated core method names to reflect the shift from simple session management to a full Identity Guard security model.",
